; === Zyl Module Resolver (self-hosted) ===
;
; The full `(use ...)` transitive-resolution logic that used to live here
; (module loading, dependency worklist, shadowing) is DEAD CODE from the
; self-hosted boot pipeline's perspective: driver.zyl's boot-run never
; calls anything in this file — assemble.py handles module concatenation
; at BUILD time instead, so runtime `(use ...)` resolution is unused by
; the bootstrap. It was removed after an extensive chase confirmed it was
; blocking the self-hosted compiler's own boot process at LINK time with
; an undefined `rbp0` symbol, despite never executing: the self-hosted
; compiler's reachability analysis is less aggressive than the Rust
; bootstrap's, so unreachable code here still got fully compiled. Root
; cause wasn't pinned down (every `set!` target name read back as an
; empty string by ICNF-lowering time despite parsing correctly — doesn't
; fit this session's other confirmed bug classes), and since the whole
; module resolution feature isn't wired into the boot path at all, there
; was nothing worth keeping half-broken. See git history to revive it.
;
; shd/stl (head/tail, like car/cdr) are kept — codegen.zyl depends on them.

(defn shd (xs)
  (match xs
    (Cons h _ h)
    (Nil "")))

(defn stl (xs)
  (match xs
    (Cons _ t t)
    (Nil Nil)))
